# tally 2.1.8 §4 item 1 (#159), L §5.19 gap and L §8.1: gap is the reading less the booked balance at its instant; at a
# reading before the run's start (2026-02-10 end, S 2026-03-01) the booked balance is the run's hole, so the gap is
# HOLE-PRERUN (g1). With no reading that day it stays HOLE-NOREADING (g2). 2.1.7's refcore gave g1 HOLE-NOREADING
# too, since the walk sees no reading outside [S, E]. The plan's p16 g2.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input keep: money PLN
input d_save: date
input go: bool

move save: transfers
  on d_save
  reads konto
  when go
  leg cash from konto to sav amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto) - keep)

move mm[m in months]: transfers
  on end_of(m) - 1 day
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to sav amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto) - keep)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  keep = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d_save = 2026-03-18 "s"
  go = true "s"
  opening[konto] = 1050.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03..2026-05
  known 2026-01-02
  anchor konto
  stated[konto] = 90.00 PLN at 2026-02-10 end "saldo"

ask g1: gap(konto, 2026-02-10)
ask g2: gap(konto, 2026-02-11)
=== expect
g1: ?"before the run's start" (konto)
  cut 2026-06-10
g2: ?"stated[konto] has no reading at 2026-02-11" (stated[konto])
  cut 2026-06-10
warning: WARN-UNREAD place world is read by nothing
